<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tzath I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tzath I was king of Lazica in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in the early 6th century. In 522 he went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, rejecting Sasanian overlordship, and was baptised and crowned by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justin-i">Justin I</a>, who gave him a Roman noblewoman as his wife. His conversion made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> the official religion of Lazica and drew it into the Byzantine sphere, one of the causes of renewed war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>.</p></div>
